{"findings":[
  {
    "id":"f01",
    "criterion":"Include your location on resumes and portfolio pages so recruiters can quickly assess fit.",
    "detail":"The portfolio identifies Nathan Phillips and his title but does not show a city, state, country or any other location indicator, despite the page being the primary application-facing profile.",
    "contested":false,
    "citations":[
      {"video_id":"fD0E57QYSPk","start_seconds":522.8,"quote":"this is one of the most important things a recruiter is going to look for in your application"},
      {"video_id":"dQ6RNltrXro","start_seconds":320.3,"quote":"add your role and location"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id":"f02",
    "criterion":"Quantify contributions with concrete metrics and outcomes.",
    "detail":"The portfolio leads with numbers (9/9, 77.1%, 10,250 predictions, 6.1x) and each project states a metric, directly matching the advice to quantify impact.",
    "contested":false,
    "citations":[
      {"video_id":"fD0E57QYSPk","start_seconds":847.5,"quote":"quantifiable numbers for every single thing you've done at a company"},
      {"video_id":"dQ6RNltrXro","start_seconds":320.3,"quote":"quantify your contributions by using metrics and data to Showcase your impact"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id":"f03",
    "criterion":"Link to detailed project write-ups or case studies, not just code repositories.",
    "detail":"Every selected system includes a 'Case study →' link, following the recommended pattern of making project understanding easy for a recruiter rather than forcing them to read code.",
    "contested":false,
    "citations":[
      {"video_id":"FpW8aiJPvts","start_seconds":333.7,"quote":"writing an accompanying blog post to the project just makes understanding your experience and skills much easier"},
      {"video_id":"ZqqzBCg6IGU","start_seconds":70.1,"quote":"Every project should have a one-page report or drive PDF link in your resume which should have what problem did you solve in this project, what text you used, what challenges did you face and what did you learn from those challenges"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id":"f04",
    "criterion":"Prefer intuitive metrics and explain technical scores that a recruiter may not know.",
    "detail":"Most metrics are intuitive counts and percentages, but '84.5% best answer F1' and '0.93 answer parity' are used without plain-language explanation, which is the kind of metric the expert warns can be lost on a recruiter.",
    "contested":false,
    "citations":[
      {"video_id":"FpW8aiJPvts","start_seconds":333.7,"quote":"a success rate of 95% is very intuitive an F1 score of 39 is perhaps not that intuitive if he doesn't know what that is"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id":"f05",
    "criterion":"Present a focused specialism instead of spreading across too many different areas.",
    "detail":"The portfolio spans agents, RAG, multi-agent, data, data-viz, and a GAN-inspired coding harness; even within an AI focus, this breadth risks watering down the positioning.",
    "contested":false,
    "citations":[
      {"video_id":"fD0E57QYSPk","start_seconds":1061.5,"quote":"not specializing in too many different things it'll sort of water your application down"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id":"f06",
    "criterion":"List concrete tools and how you apply them, not abstract subject labels only.",
    "detail":"The page highlights categories like 'agentic systems' and 'RAG pipelines' but has no skills section showing concrete technologies such as Python libraries, deployment tools, or cloud services; some tools only appear inside project descriptions.",
    "contested":false,
    "citations":[
      {"video_id":"ZqqzBCg6IGU","start_seconds":140.6,"quote":"Write how you apply that knowledge. You can write like Python having numpy pandas and psychic libraries deployment using flask and fast API cloud using AWS EC2 and S3."}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id":"f07",
    "criterion":"Keep formatting clean and free of typos because small presentation details signal professionalism.",
    "detail":"The visible portfolio is visually clean, consistently aligned, and contains no obvious typos, satisfying the formatting advice.",
    "contested":false,
    "citations":[
      {"video_id":"ZqqzBCg6IGU","start_seconds":140.6,"quote":"avoid the messy alignment, random fund sizes, grammatical mistakes. These are small things but they scream unprofessional"}
    ]
  }
]}

{"findings": [
  {
    "id": "f01",
    "criterion": "Include the applicant's location in the header or contact block, since recruiters treat it as one of the most important fields.",
    "detail": "The page opens with name, title, GitHub and LinkedIn, but no city or country appears anywhere in the header or body.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {"video_id": "fD0E57QYSPk", "start_seconds": 522.8, "quote": "another big thing that is lacking here is his location this is one of the most important things a recruiter is going to look for in your application"},
      {"video_id": "3pFRqPqzBCM", "start_seconds": 115.2, "quote": "Add LinkedIn, GitHub, location, no photo, no graphics, no tagline."}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f02",
    "criterion": "Quantify major achievements with concrete numbers, including before/after or success-rate style metrics.",
    "detail": "The portfolio leads with quantified results ('9/9 red-team attacks stopped', '77.1% eval-verified accuracy, up from 73.0%', '10,250 predictions scored', '6.1× fewer tokens at 0.93 answer parity') and each project card carries its own number.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {"video_id": "fD0E57QYSPk", "start_seconds": 847.5, "quote": "you have somehow quantifiable numbers for every single thing you've done at a company"},
      {"video_id": "dQ6RNltrXro", "start_seconds": 320.3, "quote": "quantify your contributions by using metrics and data to Showcase your impact"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f03",
    "criterion": "Prefer intuitive metrics over jargon-heavy ones like F1, or explain the metric so a recruiter understands it.",
    "detail": "The CUAD Legal Agent card uses '84.5% best answer F1' without defining what F1 measures, which is the kind of non-intuitive metric this advice cautions against.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {"video_id": "FpW8aiJPvts", "start_seconds": 333.7, "quote": "many metrics are also more intuitive for the recruiter a success rate of 95% is very intuitive an F1 score of 39 is perhaps not that intuitive if he doesn't know what that is"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f04",
    "criterion": "Attach a live, professional link to every serious project, such as a GitHub repo, live site, or case study.",
    "detail": "Every project card links to a 'Case study →' page, and the site provides GitHub and LinkedIn links in the header and footer, matching the 'prove them' advice rather than only naming projects.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {"video_id": "ZqqzBCg6IGU", "start_seconds": 70.1, "quote": "Attach a GitHub link for every serious project you have done and please make it look professional"},
      {"video_id": "fD0E57QYSPk", "start_seconds": 900.9, "quote": "if you have any links to anything that might be live like a GitHub repo or the actual website that you worked on that is a huge bonus point"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f05",
    "criterion": "Keep the document razor-focused on one target job title and one clear specialisation.",
    "detail": "The site is titled 'applied-ai', the headline says 'Applied AI Engineer', and every project/filter (Agents, RAG, Multi-agent, Data) reinforces that single specialty.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {"video_id": "by8wrrXW3So", "start_seconds": 1047.5, "quote": "You need to be razor focused on the job title that you want."},
      {"video_id": "fD0E57QYSPk", "start_seconds": 1061.5, "quote": "not specializing in too many different things it'll sort of water your application down"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f06",
    "criterion": "Describe skills as applied tools and technologies, not as generic academic subject names.",
    "detail": "The site names concrete tools and methods throughout (AWS App Runner, Slack bot, SQL, ETL, sha256 manifests, D3, GAN) instead of listing generic labels like 'Machine Learning'.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {"video_id": "ZqqzBCg6IGU", "start_seconds": 140.6, "quote": "In your skill section in resume don't write things like machine learning or statistics under skills that is knowledge not a skill. Write how you apply that knowledge."}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f07",
    "criterion": "Use the actual keywords from the target job description in the summary and skills areas.",
    "detail": "The page is rich in target keywords for applied AI roles: agentic systems, RAG pipelines, eval harnesses, red-team, SQL, AWS, and data.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {"video_id": "fD0E57QYSPk", "start_seconds": 1061.5, "quote": "making sure that you use the actual keywords that you think are important from the job in the actual description of your summary and maybe your skills"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f08",
    "criterion": "Explain each project like a product: state the problem, the technology, the challenges, and what you learned.",
    "detail": "The project cards are framed as case studies with outcomes, and the CUAD Legal Agent card explicitly reports the 'honest finding — full context won', showing challenge/learning rather than homework-style completion.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {"video_id": "ZqqzBCg6IGU", "start_seconds": 70.1, "quote": "explain your project like a product, not like a homework. Every project should have a one-page report or drive PDF link in your resume which should have what problem did you solve in this project, what text you used, what challenges did you face and what did you learn from those challenges."}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f09",
    "criterion": "Use standardized, consistent date formatting and show the timeline of work so recruiters can judge recency.",
    "detail": "The project cards and 'Earlier work' section do not display dates or any most-recent-first ordering, so a recruiter cannot tell when the work was done.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {"video_id": "_MT4SgfQ8QY", "start_seconds": 310.6, "quote": "I notice is the standardized date format"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f10",
    "criterion": "Include an education section with GPA, relevant coursework, and notable activities when applicable.",
    "detail": "The landing page contains no visible education section; if the linked About page does not provide one, it omits a section these experts consistently expect.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {"video_id": "fD0E57QYSPk", "start_seconds": 900.9, "quote": "if your GPA is pretty good you want to add your education and your GPA"},
      {"video_id": "fD0E57QYSPk", "start_seconds": 900.9, "quote": "you can also add relevant course work which I guess could be cool"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f11",
    "criterion": "Proofread the finished document and check spacing and formatting, because small errors read as unprofessional.",
    "detail": "The landing page contains visible spacing typos: '9/9red-team attacks stopped at the guardrail gate' and '6.1×fewer tokens at 0.93 answer parity' are missing spaces after the number/symbol.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {"video_id": "ZqqzBCg6IGU", "start_seconds": 140.6, "quote": "avoid the messy alignment, random fund sizes, grammatical mistakes. These are small things but they scream unprofessional"}
    ]
  }
]}
